> I've thought about what a cartoonists jam would be like, and gotten
> as far as realizing that the easiest way to organize it would be
> one cartoonist per character plus one for the background and maybe
> one for lighting, but none of this gets to the hard part--what
> would the controls be like? I'd be interested in whatever ideas
> people have.

I've long figured that puppeteering will make a big renaissance with
VR.  Cartoonists draw the basic 3D character, then visual programmers
give it controls that allow the puppeteer to give the character
appropriate facial expressions, limb movements, etc.  Most
of these controls are inherited from previous puppets, 
as per object oriented programming.  The various scenes and
characters can then be integrated into a VR puppetoon(tm).

This new art form would combined the flexibility of animation
with the sophisticated facial expressions and gestures of good
puppeteering.  Puppetoon performances might be live or constructed
in a studio, scene by scene.  Player control of puppetoons might
form the basis of advanced VR games.  

